  "id": "DrugBank_DB00694 - MONDO_19457",
  "verbalization": "Daunorubicin is associated with Therapy Related Acute Myeloid Leukemia And Myelodysplastic Syndrome through a chain of indications that link it to Decitabine, a drug commonly used in the treatment of myelodysplastic syndromes. The evidence suggests that Daunorubicin may be repurposed for this condition, as it shares a common pathway with other drugs like Ivosidenib, which also has indications for the same syndrome. The presence of Decitabine in the chain indicates a potential role in the pathophysiology of the syndrome, possibly through mechanisms involving DNA damage and cell cycle regulation. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible dependency on drugs that target similar biological processes, suggesting a broader therapeutic context for Daunorubicin in this disease.",
